The ISBN-13 check digit is the last digit, chosen so a weighted sum of all 13 digits is divisible by 10.

`toIsbn13` builds the first 12 digits as `978` plus the first 9 digits of a valid ISBN-10, then computes the check digit from those 12:

```26:29:src/isbn.mjs
  const body = "978" + s.slice(0, 9);
  let sum = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < 12; i++) sum += (i % 2 === 0 ? 1 : 3) * Number(body[i]);
  return body + ((10 - (sum % 10)) % 10);
```

Odd positions (1st, 3rd, 5th, …) are multiplied by 1 and even positions by 3, counting from the left. The check digit is `(10 - (sum % 10)) % 10`. The extra `% 10` turns a remainder of 0 into check digit 0.

For `0306406152`, the body is `978030640615`. That weighted sum is 93, `93 % 10` is 3, and `(10 - 3) % 10` is 7, so the ISBN-13 is `9780306406157`.

Validation uses the same weights on all 13 digits, including the check digit, and accepts the number only when the total is divisible by 10:

```18:20:src/isbn.mjs
  let sum = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < 13; i++) sum += (i % 2 === 0 ? 1 : 3) * Number(s[i]);
  return sum % 10 === 0;
```

